      "text": "### Deploy prerequisites: Configure 2×400G breakout on switches"
    },
    "upgradeDecision": {
      "path": "/Users/asharma/GIT-REPO/Cisco-AI-PODs-DEV/02-backend-fabric-nxos/docs/MOP-02-1-backend-fabric-sg2-deploy.md",
      "line": 22,
      "text": "- If an upgrade is required, the target NX-OS software image (per the HW&SW compatibility matrix in [Table X]{custom-style=\"Highlight\"}) should be staged on an SCP/SFTP server, such as the AI POD automation node. This server should be reachable from Nexus Dashboard, and the SHA-512 of the NX-OS image matches the digest published on cisco.com."
    },
    "reload": {
      "path": "/Users/asharma/GIT-REPO/Cisco-AI-PODs-DEV/02-backend-fabric-nxos/docs/MOP-02-1-backend-fabric-sg2-deploy.md",
      "line": 203,
      "text": "Nexus Dashboard discovers and onboards backend switches using out-of-band management (`mgmt0`) connectivity. The edge-facing fabric interfaces do not need to be up during discovery, but all core-facing links should ideally be connected correctly, with breakouts configured. Also, adding switches triggers a greenfield reload that erases all prior switch configuration except the switch hostname, management IP address, default gateway, and boot variables. Interface breakout configuration is also retained. The reload and configuration behaviour is determined by the **Add switches without reload** (default = disabled) template settings and **Preserve config** variable (greyed out/cannot be changed) in the **Add Switches/Discovery** page."
    },
    "bfdVerification": {
      "path": "/Users/asharma/GIT-REPO/Cisco-AI-PODs-DEV/02-backend-fabric-nxos/docs/MOP-02-1-backend-fabric-sg2-deploy.md",
      "line": 472,
      "text": "2. If BFD was enabled in the optional BFD procedure, confirm the BFD sessions on the underlay are up."
    }
  },
